    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d763">

                <pb facs="0266" n="1316" xml:id="pg1316"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">690D.91/3–2453</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of State to the
                        President</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d763-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-03-24">March 24, 1953</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kashmir</hi></p>
                <p>The Kashmir situation is becoming increasingly acute and war between India and
                    Pakistan is a not remote possibility. The UN effort has bogged down. Would you
                    think that Paul Hoffman might go on a private mission to explore confidentially
                    the attitude of the two parties to some partition of Kashmir? It would seem that
                    such a project might be acceptable and it is the only solution which now seems
                    to have practicable possibilities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Foster
                    Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
